# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Encyclopedia descriptions, batch P (DeepSeek)."""
DESC_P = {
    'KW:DSC2': {
        4: "The Innocent are humans possessing advanced science and technology who live in domed cities called Points. They give Walker Machines to the Civilians and purchase the Blue Stones they mine. Their ancestors were humans who fled into space to escape the great catastrophe that struck Earth. When they returned after time had passed, what they saw was the ruined land of Zora. It had become an infinitely dangerous planet for them, where exposure to the outside air for even a few hours meant death. So they created the new humanity, the Civilians, adapted to Zora's environment, as successors to carry on their civilization. They also succeeded in teaching them economics through trade in Blue Stones, which were worthless to the Innocent, and order through the Law of Three Days. Fearing that the rise of these Civilians would cost the Innocent their dominance over Zora, Kasim King repeatedly suppressed them through resistance organizations. But Jiron and the others, who overcame even that crisis, finally overturned the Innocent's system of rule. The Innocent seemed destined for extinction, but through research they developed technology that allowed them to live outside the domes as well. From then on, both peoples came to live together hand in hand.",
        5: "Arthur is the supreme leader of the Innocent. His full name is Arthur Rank, a name passed down through generations of Innocent leaders. He was confined to Yop Point by his aide Kasim King. When Jiron and the others rescued him, he saw potential in them and entrusted them with Zora's future. Later, to save Elche, who had been implanted with Kasim's consciousness, he transferred Kasim's consciousness into himself. This transformed him into a ferocious personality, but he summoned his Final Power and leaped from the Iron Gear with a bomb, dying in the explosion... or so it seemed, but in the theatrical version he revived as if nothing had happened after everything was over, sending his guard into raptures.",
        7: "The Titans are a special forces unit of the Earth Federation Forces composed of elites from Earth. The current commander-in-chief is Jamitov Hyman. They were established in U.C. 0083 for the purpose of monitoring Spacenoids, following the Zeon remnant force's colony drop operation 'Stardust'. In reality, however, they were an organization created to oppress Spacenoids, and would not hesitate to commit mass murder of colony residents with poison gas if necessary. The soldiers belonging to it were intoxicated by their power, and became steeped in arrogance, boasting things like 'The Titans outrank regular soldiers by two grades'. But after repeated conflicts with the AEUG and Axis, the organization's upper echelons were annihilated, and it was effectively dissolved. The war between the AEUG and the Titans that took place in U.C. 0087 is called the 'Gryps Conflict'.",
        8: "The AEUG is a military organization formed around Major General Blex Forer, who was also a member of the Earth Federation Congress, to oppose the tyranny of the Titans. Its official name is 'Anti Earth Union Government'. Receiving Mobile Suit supplies from its sponsor, Anaheim Electronics, it resisted the Titans who oppressed Spacenoids. Many people other than soldiers participated, sharing the same ideals, but the AEUG was, after all, an organization within the Earth Federation Forces. For this reason, some viewed the conflict between the two as nothing more than an internal rebellion within the military. It held a cooperative relationship with the Earth-based anti-Federation organization Karaba, and joint operations by the two dealt heavy blows to the Titans' ground forces. After Blex was assassinated, Quattro Bageena, otherwise known as Char Aznable, rose as their leader and exposed the Titans' misdeeds at the Dakar Federation Congress.",
        14: "Gendarme is a dome city on the lunar surface, serving as the capital of the Moonrace's living sphere. The Ghingnham family built it and also serves as its guardian. The White Palace, the castle of Queen Dianna Soreil, and the Winter Palace, an artificial hibernation facility where many citizens sleep, are also located here. In addition, records of the Dark History remain beneath the Winter Palace, and it was here that the threat of civilization's collapse by the M-Fly was made clear.",
        18: "A political organization known for its extremism. All of its members are Naturals, and under the slogan 'For a blue and pure world,' they aim to exclude Coordinators. Among Naturals, there are many who, even if they do not participate in Blue Cosmos, view Coordinators with suspicion. This is also a result of their manipulation of consciousness.\nHowever, the political organization is only a public face; in the shadows, they conceal their aspect as a secret society that acts as the agent of LOGOS in order to achieve the extermination of Coordinators. This is possible because their members have infiltrated even the upper echelons of the Atlantic Federation and the Earth Alliance Forces.\nAfter the death of their leader Muruta Azrael in the Second Battle of Jachin Due in C.E. 71, they lay low for a while. But when Lord Djibril assumed the position of new leader, they once again manipulated public opinion by moving the Atlantic Federation and the mass media to lead the Earth Alliance and PLANT into war.\nHowever, due to Durandal's accusation, the organization's upper echelons were destroyed along with LOGOS. Their activities were forced into a large-scale reduction.",
        19: 'A military-industrial complex said to have existed since the dawn of history, holding strong power to intervene in politics. It is composed of merchants of death who have manipulated war and reconstruction from behind the scenes and amassed enormous profits.\nIt is the support base of Blue Cosmos, and it guided public opinion to provoke wars between the Earth Alliance and Coordinators. Muruta Azrael, the former leader of Blue Cosmos, and Lord Djibril, the current leader, are also members of LOGOS. For LOGOS, the goal is to continue war and pursue profit; the fact that Blue Cosmos advocates the extermination of Coordinators is largely due to the personal feelings of these two men.\nBecause they possess no military strength of their own, in the previous war they attempted to annihilate Coordinators by moving the Earth Alliance Forces. And after the war, they organized Phantom Pain to exercise power more directly.\nLater, because their existence and deeds were exposed by Durandal, most of their members were arrested or died from lynchings due to riots of angry citizens. Djibril, who survived to the very end, had his trump card, Requiem, taken away, and was shot down along with his fleeing ship.',
        25: "A military PLANT that ZAFT maintains in the L4 sphere.\nIt was developing the 'Second Stage' mobile suits, typified by the Impulse, as well as the new warship Minerva, which would operate them.\nHowever, on the day of the Minerva's launch ceremony, it was subjected to a surprise attack by the Earth Alliance special task force 'Phantom Pain,' and all of the 'Second Stage' units except the Impulse were seized.",
        26: "The capital of PLANT, located in the L5 sphere.\nAt the end of the war, it was made the target of the large strategic beam cannon 'Requiem' by the madness-consumed Djibril. However, thanks to the efforts of the Joule team, the line of fire was deflected and it avoided annihilation. Nevertheless, the surrounding PLANTs suffered severe damage.",
        28: "The United Emirates of Orb. A small nation located in the Pacific Ocean, composed of several islands.\nIt is a rare place where Naturals and Coordinators coexist peacefully, and it declares a stance of neutrality, aligning with neither the Alliance nor ZAFT. It maintains Morgenroete, Inc. as a public enterprise.\nIt also declared neutrality in the previous war, but its homeland was scorched by war due to the Earth Alliance's invasion. Although its means of living were rebuilt after the war, the fact that a large number of skilled people left due to the war's effects is a headache for the current representative head of state, Cagalli Yula Athha.\nEven so, it is difficult for the young Cagalli to seize the initiative, and the schemes of the five great families that lead the nation are in disarray within. In particular, the head of the Seiran family, the chancellor Unato, is strongly power-hungry, and plots to have his son Yuna marry Cagalli to control the government as he pleases. Furthermore, he conspired with LOGOS, abandoned the ideal of neutrality, and concluded an alliance with the Earth Alliance.\nBut that honeymoon was also brought to an end by Cagalli, who returned with the Archangel, and Orb returned once again to its former neutral state.",
        33: "Rau Le Creuset. An excellent military officer who serves as a commander in ZAFT. In truth, he is a Natural, but he concealed this fact and enlisted in ZAFT. He was born as a clone of Mu's father, Al Da Flaga, but because the telomeres that govern lifespan were shorter than normal, he was treated as a defective product. Upon learning of this fact, he came to despise the world itself that had produced a being like himself. Eventually, in order to bring both ZAFT and the Alliance to mutual destruction, he leaked operation plans and transferred military secrets. As a result, his schemes had reached the brink of success by the time of the Second Battle of Yakin Due. However, he was defeated in battle against the Freedom, and, cursing the world, vanished into the light of the runaway Genesis. Because he regularly used a special drug that slowed aging, he was occasionally seen suffering from side effects. It is thought that he always hid his face behind a mask in order to conceal a face that had aged beyond his years, along with his hidden dark ambitions. He came to know Ray Za Burrel, who was also a clone of Al Da Flaga, through his old friend Durandal, and took it upon himself to act as Ray's guardian.",
        34: 'A wartime treaty concluded between the Earth Alliance and PLANT on March 10, C.E. 72, the year after the previous war ended. It was signed at Junius Seven, where the scars of the previous war remained deep, and so it received this name. Its main purpose was the limitation of armaments, establishing caps on the number of mobile suits possessed and prohibiting the use of Neutron Jammer Cancellers. It also included the restoration of border lines, and nations that had been annexed by the Earth Alliance during the war, such as the Orb Union of Chiefdoms, recovered their independence. However, since each faction was secretly developing weapons that violated the treaty, it could be said that, at least in military terms, it had become a dead letter.',
        35: "Enhanced humans developed by the Alliance under the leadership of Blue Cosmos. They were deployed on the mission to seize the 'Second Stage Series' at Armory One. They improved upon the problems of the earlier enhanced humans, the 'Biological CPUs,' who had been emotionally unstable, and succeeded in maintaining abilities capable of fighting on par with or above Coordinators while also granting them enough coordination to operate as a team. However, if they hear a block word set as a safety device, they fall into an extremely unstable mental state. Furthermore, after combat, maintenance using an adjustment machine called the 'Cradle' is indispensable. The 'Cradle' also possesses a memory adjustment function, and it was used to erase the memories of Stella, who had become MIA, from the other two.",
        40: 'A 3D versus fighting game in which one battles by piloting Overmen. It is also possible to engage in simultaneous multiplayer matches online. At the beginning of the story, Gainer achieves 200 consecutive victories and earns the title of King. Also, as special training against the Overdevil, Gainer undertakes the severe practice of fighting simultaneously in both reality and the game. He splendidly downs 200 machines in both arenas and even earns the title of First King.',
        42: "Rock that rises in multiple layers like scabs. Its colorful appearance resembles coral, and so it received this name. It is also simply called 'Scab.' Because it occurs in all sorts of places, in human living areas, giant piles called 'Pile Bunkers' are driven deep into the earth to prevent uplifting. Beneath the scab, archetypes of LFOs and KLFs are buried. For this reason, many excavators continue to dig deep underground. Eventually, Dr. Bear puts forth the hypothesis that the Scub Coral is a sentient being, and this turns out to be true. And what the Scub Coral sent as a messenger to humanity was the humanoid Coralian, which was the hope for humanity and the Scub Coral to coexist.",
        47: "An elite special forces unit of the Tower State Federation military. It officially adopted the Terminus type R505 painted in blue. Holland, Eureka, and Charles and Ray were all members at one time.\nThey were involved in the massacre of believers at the sacred site of Vodarac, which became the catalyst for Holland's desertion from the military. It was also at this time that Eureka picked up Maurice and the other two children.",
        49: "A highly popular accessory brand.\nTalho was a big fan of it, and she pestered Holland into buying her a reissued silver ring. The ring was crushed in a battle that broke out shortly afterward, but in the end, the bond between the two grew even stronger.\nLater, the ring was transformed by Holland's hands into an engagement ring, and it shone on their ring fingers as a symbol connecting the two of them.",
    },
}
